atches a uniform distribution on the unit interval?","options":["Values from a pseudo-random number generator on $[0,1]$","The number of calls arriving in ten minutes","The number of successes before replacement","The number of failures before the first success."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"d22fdea3d6380c42d039e5e0"},{"id":"pt_batch7_uniform_distribution_011","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Why do equal-length subintervals inside $[a,b]$ have equal probability?","options":["The density is largest at the midpoint","The density is constant on the support interval","The endpoints have positive mass","The support contains only finitely many values"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"37df059f506934e653972b6d"},{"id":"pt_batch7_uniform_distribution_012","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"How can $P(c\\le X\\le d)$ be found for $X\\sim U(a,b)$ when $[c,d]\\subseteq[a,b]$?","options":["By multiplying the endpoint values $cd$","By using the number of integers between $c$ and $d$.","By dividing the subinterval length $d-c$ by the total length $b-a$","By adding $a+b+c+d$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"eb9d82b48a8ebbd9021ae5c0"},{"id":"pt_batch7_uniform_distribution_013","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Why is the uniform distribution useful in simulation?","options":["Uniform variables are always discrete counts.","Uniform variables avoid using probabilities","Uniform variables only generate endpoints","Uniform variables are inputs for inverse transform methods"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"69895cd05cb2bf2f2f5cff8c"},{"id":"pt_batch7_uniform_distribution_014","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"If $X\\sim U(10,20)$, what is $P(12\\le X\\le17)$?","options":["$1/5$","$7/10$","$0$","$1/2$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"9f0971de784d13026e21ccfa"},{"id":"pt_batch7_uniform_distribution_015","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"If $X\\sim U(-2,2)$, what is $E[X]$?","options":["$2$","$-2$","$1/4$","$0$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"42f1125db0a2886e392cf4a8"},{"id":"pt_batch7_uniform_distribution_016","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"If $X\\sim U(3,7)$, what is the density on $[3,7]$?","options":["$4$","$1/10$","$1/4$","$5$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"1b5c6466ed92cc0676d9d1c7"},{"id":"pt_batch7_uniform_distribution_017","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"For $X\\sim U(a,b)$, why does changing from $[c,d]$ to $(c,d)$ not change the probability?","options":["The density outside $[a,b]$ becomes negative","The open interval always has probability zero.","The mean changes to $(c+d)/2$","The endpoints have probability zero in this distribution"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"9e93b8958ab4b21c3bbe713b"},{"id":"pt_batch7_uniform_distribution_018","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"What does 'uniform' guarantee for intervals inside the support?","options":["Intervals of the same length have the same probability","Every subset with the same number of written symbols has the same probability","The density is highest near $a$","The variable takes only the midpoint"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"6a49d1d7847356b6c44fdbe3"},{"id":"pt_batch7_uniform_distribution_019","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"If $X\\sim U(0,10)$, what is $P(X=5)$?","options":["$1/10$","$1/5$","$1$","$0$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"71e2fe0f75e3b0c800f99491"},{"id":"pt_batch7_uniform_distribution_020","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"If $X\\sim U(0,8)$, compare $P(1\\le X\\le3)$ and $P(4\\le X\\le6)$.","options":["They are equal","The first is twice the second","The second is twice the first","Both are necessarily zero"],"answer_